WEBVTT

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:14.450
Excuse me, officer.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:15.760
Can you help me?

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.120
Sure.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.580
Can you tell me

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.760
how to get to Linden Street, in Riverdale?

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.140
"Richard Stewart, 46 Linden Street,

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.160
Riverdale, New York."

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.880
You should take the number 1 subway.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.760
Is there a station near here?

00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.300
Yes. The station's that way.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.930
You should take the number 1 train

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:31.040
to Van Cortlandt Park.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:34.340
Number 1 train to Van Cortlandt Park. Thank you.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.480
Anytime. Good luck.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.900
Remember, the number 1 train. The uptown platform.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:39.660
Thank you.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:58.840
Is this pink too bright for me?

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.820
Mmm-hmm. It is a very bright pink.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.460
Try this. It's size eight.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:15.940
But I wear size ten.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:21.400
How about green? It's size ten.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.380
Let me try it on.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.000
I'm taking too much of your time.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.040
It's six o'clock.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.120
Where's my husband?

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:34.760
I was expecting him here at five forty-five.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.220
Don't worry. The traffic is very heavy at this hour.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.400
I know. But we're going to be late for dinner.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:43.280
I'll take this green sweater.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.660
I like the color on me, don't you?

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.420
I think it looks terrific on you.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.620
I'm sorry I'm so late.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:54.900
I had a really bad day.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.260
It's ten after six. We're late.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.640
Robbie's cooking tonight, and dinner's at six thirty.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.880
I know. I know. I'm really sorry.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.580
I left my bag of film on the ferry.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:08.220
I went back for it, but the ferry was gone.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:09.680
I lost a whole day's work.

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:13.060
I'll call the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:14.800
I didn't think of that. Thanks.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:21.880
Hello.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:24.030
Yes. The number, please,

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.900
of the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.900
Five five five...zero eight zero eight.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:36.360
Thank you.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.500
I really appreciate it, Marilyn.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.060
Hello.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.780
Did anyone find a camera bag this afternoon,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.340
a small canvas bag,

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:54.060
on the J. F. Kennedy Ferry?...No?

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.800
Maybe someone will find it.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:00.640
The name is Stewart, Richard Stewart.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.740
And the telephone number is five five five...

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:09.020
three oh nine oh. Thank you.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.640
Sorry, Richard. They don't have it.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:14.840
Thanks, anyway.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.280
There was a girl on the ferry.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.100
Tell me about it on the way home.
